"identically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:235
msgid ""
"Other native tools advertised by OpenAI (file search, code interpreter) "
"are not available in the System Console for Google providers — only Web "
"Search is offered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:237
msgid ""
"If a feature surface uses **NativeWebSearchAllowed** at request time (for"
" example, the in-product web-search shortcut), Bifrost adds web search to"
" the Gemini Responses request even if the agent has not explicitly "
"checked **Web Search** under Native Google Tools. This is how the plugin "
"lets a single feature toggle web search on without forcing every agent to"
" enable it manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:239
#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:327
msgid "Example service configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:260
msgid ""
"Vertex AI provides access to Gemini and other Google models through "
"Google Cloud's enterprise AI platform, with project-scoped billing, "
"regional deployment, and IAM-based access control. Like the direct Gemini"
" integration, Vertex AI is routed through Bifrost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:262
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:264
msgid "Before configuring the service in Mattermost, complete this in GCP:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:266
msgid ""
"**Have or create a Google Cloud project.** Note the **Project ID** (slug,"
" e.g., `my-project-123`) and the **Project Number** (numeric, e.g., "
"`123456789012`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:267
msgid ""
"**Enable the Vertex AI API** for that project: `gcloud services enable "
"aiplatform.googleapis.com --project <PROJECT_ID>` or the equivalent in "
"the GCP Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:268
msgid ""
"**Choose a region** that has the Vertex models you need (for example, "
"`us-central1`, `us-east5`, `europe-west4`). Model availability varies by "
"region — check [Vertex AI model availability](https://cloud.google.com"
"/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/locations) before committing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:269
msgid "**Decide your authentication mode** — see below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:273
msgid "The plugin supports two authentication modes via Bifrost:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:275
msgid ""
"**Application Default Credentials (ADC)** — recommended when the plugin "
"runs on GCP (GKE, GCE, Cloud Run) with an attached service account, or "
"when the host's `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` environment variable "
"points at a service-account key file. Leave the **Service Account JSON** "
"field blank to use ADC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:276
msgid ""
"**Service Account JSON** — paste the full contents of a service-account "
"key JSON into the **Service Account JSON** field. The plugin validates "
"that the field contains valid JSON before saving. The service account "
"needs `roles/aiplatform.user` (or a custom role with the "
"`aiplatform.endpoints.predict` permission) in your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:278
msgid "To create a service-account key for the JSON path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:280
msgid ""
"In the GCP Console, go to **IAM & Admin > Service Accounts** and create a"
" service account (or pick an existing one)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:281
msgid "Grant the account `roles/aiplatform.user` on the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:282
msgid ""
"Open the service account, go to **Keys > Add Key > Create new key**, "
"choose **JSON**, and download the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:283
msgid ""
"Open the downloaded file, copy its full contents (including braces), and "
"paste into the **Service Account JSON** field in Mattermost. Treat this "
"file as a secret — anyone with it can call Vertex against your project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:285
msgid ""
"Bifrost stores the JSON as a credential. When **Service Account JSON** is"
" empty, Bifrost falls back to ADC at request time — no key material is "
"held in plugin config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:289
msgid "Complete the prerequisites above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:290
msgid ""
"In Mattermost, open **System Console > Agents > LLM Services** and add a "
"new service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:291
msgid "Select **Google Vertex AI** in the **Service** dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:292
msgid ""
"Fill in **GCP Project ID**, **GCP Region**, and (optionally) **GCP "
"Project Number**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:293
msgid ""
"For ADC: leave **Service Account JSON** blank. For key-based auth: paste "
"the full JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:294
msgid ""
"Enter a model identifier in **Default Model** (for example, "
"`gemini-2.5-pro`). Use the [Vertex AI model "
"catalog](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-"
"ai/docs/learn/models) to confirm the exact Vertex model ID for your "
"region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:295
msgid "Save the service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "**GCP Project ID**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "Your Google Cloud project ID slug (e.g., `my-project-123`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "**GCP Project Number**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid ""
"Numeric project number (e.g., `123456789012`). Project Number is required"
" only when using a numeric endpoint ID for a fine-tuned model. For all "
"standard publisher models (Gemini, Claude, Mistral), Project Number is "
"not consumed and can be left blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "**GCP Region**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid ""
"Vertex AI region (e.g., `us-central1`, `europe-west4`). Model "
"availability is region-specific."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "**Service Account JSON**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid ""
"Full service-account key JSON. Validated as JSON on save. Leave blank to "
"use ADC or an attached IAM role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid ""
"The Vertex model ID to use (see [Vertex AI model "
"documentation](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-"
"ai/docs/learn/models))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "Optional override for the maximum input context size, in tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:309
msgid ""
"The **API Key**, **Send User ID**, and **Use Responses API** toggles do "
"not apply to the **Google Vertex AI** service type. The Responses API "
"path is auto-enabled when a native Google tool is in use; otherwise the "
"Chat path is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:313
msgid ""
"For Gemini models running on Vertex AI, reasoning is configured the same "
"way as direct Gemini and follows the same model-version mapping (Gemini "
"2.5 vs. 3.0+). Enable **Reasoning** on the agent and set either "
"**Thinking Budget** (tokens) or **Reasoning Effort** (minimal / low / "
"medium / high). When both are set, the explicit budget wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:315
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Anthropic Claude on Vertex.** When you select an Anthropic model ID "
"(for example, `claude-sonnet-4-6@20260101`) on a Vertex service, the "
"agent uses Anthropic-style extended thinking instead of `thinkingConfig`."
" The **Thinking Budget** field still applies; the **Reasoning Effort** "
"selector is ignored. Model IDs follow the format `{claude-model-"
"name}@{YYYYMMDD}` where the date is the Anthropic snapshot version. Check"
" the [Anthropic on Vertex AI "
"documentation](https://docs.anthropic.com/claude/reference/claude-on-"
"vertex-ai) for current versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:319
msgid ""
"Native Google tools are **off by default** for Vertex AI, matching the "
"same posture as Cohere, Mistral, and Bedrock. Enable per agent under "
"**Native Google Tools**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid "Grounds responses with Google Search via the Vertex Responses API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md
msgid ""
"When enabled, Bifrost switches to the Responses API. Citations are "
"returned alongside the response. If requests fail with grounding enabled,"
" confirm the Vertex AI API is enabled, the selected model supports "
"grounding, and your Google Cloud project satisfies Vertex AI grounding "
"prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:325
msgid ""
"OpenAI-style `file_search` and `code_interpreter` are not available in "
"the System Console for Google providers — only Web Search is offered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:349
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:351
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Saving fails with \"invalid service account JSON\".** The plugin "
"validates that the **Service Account JSON** field contains valid JSON "
"before saving. Re-copy the full contents of the key file, including the "
"surrounding `{ }`, and check there are no truncated or escaped "
"characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:352
msgid ""
"**Requests fail with `PERMISSION_DENIED`.** Confirm the service account "
"has `roles/aiplatform.user` on the project, and that the Vertex AI API is"
" enabled. For ADC deployments, confirm the bound principal (workload "
"identity, instance SA, etc.) has the same role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:353
msgid ""
"**Model not found in region.** Vertex model IDs are region-scoped. Check "
"the model is available in your **GCP Region**, or switch to a region that"
" has it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/providers.md:354
msgid ""
"**Web search returns no citations.** Confirm **Web Search** is checked "
"under **Native Google Tools** for the agent, verify the selected model "
"supports grounding, and make sure your Google Cloud project meets the "
"current Vertex AI grounding prerequisites."
msgstr ""

